  "limitations": [
    "The value of N in the path analysis was low, mainly because of participants not finishing the difficult reading paragraphs in Wave 1.",
    "Future research needs to address the importance of both the developmental timing and the duration of noise exposure in determining the effect of noise on reading and cognitive development.",
    "Research needs to sample a wider range of noise levels in order to generate a dose-response function for reading."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This longitudinal empirical study investigated the effects of chronic aircraft noise exposure on cognitive performance in schoolchildren before and after an airport switch. Findings indicate that chronic aircraft noise impaired long-term memory, reading, and speech perception in newly exposed children, while the cessation of noise led to improvements in reading, long-term memory, and short-term memory in formerly exposed children. However, speech perception deficits did not recover after noise cessation. Mediation analyses suggested that impaired recall was partially mediated by reading, but reading deficits were not mediated by speech perception. Limitations include a a low sample size for some path analyses and the need for further research on developmental timing, exposure duration, and dose-response functions.",
